    "result_text": "Green. All three findings addressed \u2014 I agreed with all of them, as they're consistent with the package's established single-source-of-truth helper convention.\n\n## What changed\n\n**New `OwnerEmail` helper** (sibling to `OwnerCity`/`OwnerAddress`/`OwnerTelephone`) now owns all email-domain logic:\n- `DISPOSABLE_DOMAINS` \u2014 the blocklist, moved here from `ValidateNewOwner`.\n- `domain(email)` \u2014 the single home for \"domain = everything after the last `@`, lower-cased\".\n- `isDisposable(email)` \u2014 exact-match blocklist check (used by `ValidateNewOwner` for its 400).\n- `isDisposableAdjacent(email)` \u2014 the soft adjacency signal (used by `FlagRisk`), with `DISPOSABLE_BASES` derived from the same blocklist.\n\n**`FlagRisk`** is now just the roll-up the review asked for \u2014 a clean three-way OR, no inlined email subsystem:\n```java\nowner.setRiskFlag(possibleDuplicate\n        || OwnerEmail.isDisposableAdjacent(owner.getEmail())\n        || overSoftCapacity);\n```\n\n**`ValidateNewOwner`** delegates to `OwnerEmail.isDisposable(canonical)` instead of its own constant and inline substring, and the now-unused `DISPOSABLE_DOMAINS` constant and `java.util.Set` import are gone.\n\nThis resolves all three findings together: the dependency now points from both steps *into* `OwnerEmail` (not from a `Flag*` step into a `Validate*` step's internals), the domain-extraction duplication is removed, and the blocklist + adjacency rule sit in one unit \u2014 exactly how `OwnerCity` already serves both `CheckCityCapacity` and `FlagCityCapacityWarning`.\n\nBehaviour is unchanged: `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
